WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.080
What's up? Welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, Episode 97 for July 9, 2026.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.380
Let's break down today's coolest AI news so anyone can understand it. Let's go.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:18.200
Open AI just rolled out something called GPT Live to people who already pay for chat GPT.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:24.100
This turns the chatbot most of us already know into a system that can see through your phone camera

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.980
and talk back in real-time with its own voice.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:32.500
Think of it like switching from texting a friend to hopping on a video call where they can watch

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.880
what you show them and answer without any delay. Instead of typing a question and waiting,

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.940
you speak naturally, and the AI listens, watches, and replies while the conversation stays smooth.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.920
Most of us already use chatbots for homework help or brainstorming ideas for school projects.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:56.240
Live voice and video makes those moments feel more like having a patient tutor right beside you

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.420
who can look at whatever you point the camera at. That shift matters because it changes how

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.780
students might practice speeches or how friends could work on creative ideas without being in the

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:12.720
same room. For you, it could mean asking the AI to guide you through fixing something on your bike

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:18.280
while you show it the parts with your camera. The feature is already live for paid users,

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.140
so open the chat GPT app on your phone, update it if needed, and tap the new Live button to start.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:31.800
No extra sign up is required if you already have a paid plan. Now for the deep dive where we look

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.720
at how this live mode actually works under the hood. Picture a group video call with friends where

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:44.200
everyone talks and the app keeps everything moving without awkward gaps. The AI does something similar,

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:50.380
except it has to understand your words instantly, decide on a reply, and speak it while also

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:56.200
watching anything you show on camera. It starts by chopping your spoken words into tiny sound

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.320
pieces it can handle quickly, like slicing a long sentence into bite-sized chunks.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:07.280
Next, it checks those pieces against everything it has learned before and picks the best response

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:13.200
based on both what you said and what the camera sees right now. It keeps a short running memory

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.000
of just the last few seconds, kind of like a sticky note that gets refreshed constantly

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:24.700
so the flow never resets. That constant back and forth speed is what makes the whole thing feel like

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:30.980
talking to a real person instead of sending messages and waiting. Once you try it, the difference between

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:36.800
typing and speaking becomes clear right away. You end up with a tool that feels alive because it

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.660
matches the natural rhythm of conversation. Okay, now let's check out some other cool tools you can

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:52.220
try today. First up is Grok 4.5 from the team at XAI. XAI just released Grok 4.5 as a new version.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:58.800
Elon Musk says the model aims to match the power of top models while staying lighter and cheaper to run.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.280
It can handle creative writing, it answers questions, it helps with everyday tasks the same way other

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:13.340
chat bots do. Anyone with an X account can try it right now for free on the X app or at grok.x.ai.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:19.240
Next is Google's deep fake detection work that recently helped spot a fake photo of a senator

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:25.500
that was spreading online. Earlier this week, a scary looking photo of Senator Mitch McConnell spread

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:32.100
online. The photo turned out to be completely made up by AI. Google's deep fake detection system

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:37.600
helped prove it was fake. The system spotted the telltale signs that human eyes miss.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:44.680
This kind of tool matters because fake images can spread fast on social media and cause real confusion.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.820
While the full detector isn't open to everyone yet, you can still practice spotting

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:55.800
fakes yourself by looking closely at lighting, shadows, and background details in photos you see online.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:01.600
Time for quick bits where we cover two smaller updates in just a few sentences each.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:08.620
Meastrol released a small model called RoboStrol Navigate. This model has 8 billion parameters.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:15.400
It guides robots through new spaces using only a single camera feed. It was trained mostly in video game

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:21.780
simulations. It was then fine-tuned with reinforcement learning. This approach could make it easier for

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:28.260
future robots to explore places they've never seen before. The company Meastrol is entering robotics

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:34.240
with this model. Amazon is also working on a new version of Alexa nicknamed MoonRaker.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:41.440
Amazon is working on a new version of Alexa nicknamed MoonRaker that can handle longer multi-step tasks.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.600
Instead of answering one question at a time, the goal is for it to plan and carry out things like

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:53.880
booking a trip. It can manage a shopping list without you giving every single instruction. It is still

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:59.040
in development. It is not available yet. Amazon is reported to be working on this more

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:04.480
powerful, agentic, assistant. And that's a wrap. If any of today's stories made you go,

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:10.440
huh? That's cool. Go play with it. Curiosity is how every expert started. See you tomorrow,

